# adlaplace

Laplace approximations for hierarchical models using CppAD (via the
**RCppAD** R package) and trust-region optimization.

## Dependencies

- **RCppAD** — `Imports` + `LinkingTo`; provides `#include <cppad/cppad.hpp>`.
  Install RCppAD before building this package. No system CppAD /
  `libcppad_lib` is required.
- **OpenMP** — recommended (`SystemRequirements: OpenMP`); configure enables
  it when available. Without OpenMP, install still works and `num_threads`
  is ignored.

## Package layout

| Layer | R | C++ |
|-------|---|-----|
| Model (formula, S4 terms) | `effects.R`, `data_setup.R`, term `*.R` | — |
| Laplace (AD handle, profile likelihood) | `ad_fun.R`, `ad_data.R`, `log_lik.R`, … | `inner_opt`, … |
| Engine (eval, optimizer) | `R/RcppExports.R` | `src/`, `src/include/adlaplace/` |

Public headers for backend packages live in `inst/include/adlaplace/`.
Private engine headers are in `src/include/adlaplace/`.

Backend packages (e.g. `adlaplaceExample`, `adlaplaceGrf`, `hpolcc`) should
also `LinkingTo` / `Imports` **RCppAD**, and typically link against the
installed `adlaplace` shared library.

See the monorepo root [`README.md`](../README.md) for install order.
